00:29:49.920 --> 00:29:51.780
Between the trees, right? Yeah.

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:59.460
Yes. But on the main screen, like the first screen that you go to, there are these tiny little paths to the left and the right.

00:29:59.580 --> 00:30:01.400
But there's a really wide path in front of you.

00:30:01.600 --> 00:30:06.120
And the way the cave is kind of almost like on an angle,

00:30:06.720 --> 00:30:10.580
it makes it so that when you leave the cave, you kind of want to keep going forward.

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:40.000
You know?

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:43.820
So I think that there are like little natural little nudges.

00:30:44.140 --> 00:30:48.680
Like the landscape kind of makes you want to check out certain things and avoid other things.

00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:53.600
And it's not like your next objective is ever like so far away from you.

00:30:53.800 --> 00:30:57.940
Your next objective is relatively well placed to where you have to go next.

00:30:58.140 --> 00:31:06.300
The game doesn't really rely on the player going from the, you know, the far southeast all the way up to the northwest.

00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:08.320
You know? Like it doesn't really happen that way.

00:31:08.320 --> 00:31:10.100
And there was a time where I tried that.

00:31:10.280 --> 00:31:13.000
And when I first started, I said, okay, I'm not going to look at the manual.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:17.480
I just, I know that there's like a map at the bottom of it just because I've heard about this game so much.

00:31:18.720 --> 00:31:19.780
I'm just going to explore.

00:31:20.180 --> 00:31:23.000
And I fought a Lionel.

00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:24.920
Oh my goodness. In one of my first playthroughs.

00:31:25.040 --> 00:31:27.140
