00:33:03.420 --> 00:33:11.640
And I think like, you know, the first one that stuck out for me was the candle because you get the blue candle from a merchant, not in a dungeon where it's dark.

00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:16.920
So you're using this thing for a while is like, oh, OK, this thing's like a flame that I can only use once.

00:33:17.260 --> 00:33:19.740
Like, you know, I'm not really sure what's going on.

00:33:19.900 --> 00:33:23.520
And then, you know, there's like a moment because you get that pretty early.

00:33:23.900 --> 00:33:27.960
And the first dungeon that does blackout, I think, isn't isn't until level four.

00:33:28.420 --> 00:33:30.120
And you get to one of those dark rooms.

00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:34.800
And the first thing I thought of was like, what if I just light the room up?

00:33:34.900 --> 00:33:36.940
Like, you know, like, why don't I just use the candle?

00:33:36.940 --> 00:33:46.900
And it's so smart to do it that way because the easier approach would have been the blue candle is the item of that dungeon in level four that you have to go find.

00:33:47.140 --> 00:33:58.700
And then that's like explicitly telling you like, hey, you know, this candle is the way to kind of like how the ladder is given to you in level five, level five or six.

00:33:58.920 --> 00:34:06.740
The ladder is given to you because it's like that's the only way you're going to be able to get across the water to finish the rest of the dungeon.

00:34:06.740 --> 00:34:07.580
Like, you need that.

00:34:07.700 --> 00:34:21.480
And that one was like, this is such a very specific use case thing that I think the ladder for me was the only item that I wasn't actually impressed by because it was it was more of a Metroid thing, you know, where it's like you can't open these doors until you get those missiles.

00:34:21.860 --> 00:34:24.580
You know, it's like you can't cross this until you get that ladder.

00:34:24.860 --> 00:34:27.400
Right. Similar to the raft, actually, too.

00:34:27.540 --> 00:34:29.000
If we can talk about the raft for a second.

00:34:29.180 --> 00:34:30.500
Yeah. That was kind of strange.

00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:32.180
I think that has a similar element.

00:34:32.180 --> 00:34:36.340
I know. I know you guys didn't care for in Rygar, which.

00:34:36.560 --> 00:34:39.440
Yeah. There's like a there's like a thing that.

00:34:39.600 --> 00:34:42.700
Oh, yeah. Trigger is like this is where you can use the grappling hook.

00:34:42.780 --> 00:34:44.500
Like this is where you can use the raft only.

00:34:44.640 --> 00:34:46.040
I'm like, but it's a raft and that's water.

00:34:46.440 --> 00:34:47.780
You can't put the raft on water.

00:34:47.920 --> 00:34:53.520
It's also weird, though, too, because you get the raft and then it's like it's not usable in the dungeon.

00:34:53.740 --> 00:34:59.240
Right. And yes, like you get it in the dungeon right before you're supposed to go to the raft dungeon.

00:34:59.620 --> 00:35:04.080
But like I wouldn't have thought like, you know, like go check that out.

00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:05.600
It's just something that's more or less going to happen.

00:35:05.840 --> 00:35:14.260
Thankfully, they didn't map it to be like it's just like as long as you have the raft in your item inventory, you can go to the level four dungeon now.

00:35:14.680 --> 00:35:19.720
But since we're talking about, you know, the order of these dungeons with them, I'm giving out crazy numbers.

00:35:20.340 --> 00:35:23.020
Nobody really like did them in the exact order.

00:35:23.260 --> 00:35:28.120
Right. Well, OK, so let me tell you a little story about how I play this game.

00:35:28.200 --> 00:35:29.820
Make this as long as it has to be.

00:35:29.900 --> 00:35:34.580
I want to hear it. OK, so I move the game, go in, get the sword.

00:35:34.920 --> 00:35:36.160
Everything's going great so far.

00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:45.420
I end up going to the west and I'm in the woods and I find my way to like a hole in the wall.

00:35:45.720 --> 00:35:49.160
And there's like an old lady and she's like, hey, give me money.

00:35:49.300 --> 00:35:52.500
I'll tell you a secret. So I'm like, I got some cash.

00:35:52.500 --> 00:35:54.380
So I pay for the rupees.

00:35:54.600 --> 00:36:00.460
I got some rupees. So I ask for the most expensive secret and she gives me some directions.

00:36:01.060 --> 00:36:09.960
And so I follow the directions to the lost woods and I have three hearts and I go right into the sixth dungeon.

00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:13.800
And I'm sort of just like taken aback by what's around me.

00:36:13.980 --> 00:36:17.120
And I get through like maybe two screens before I drop dead.

00:36:17.320 --> 00:36:21.720
Now you saw the level six thing and knew you were in the sixth dungeon or you just thought like I'm that.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:25.900
OK, I'm just making sure that you didn't think like, oh, this is the first dungeon.

00:36:26.060 --> 00:36:27.040
This is tough. Yeah.

00:36:28.180 --> 00:36:29.620
I'm like, OK, level six.

00:36:29.880 --> 00:36:34.300
I know that there's nine dungeons just from knowing about this game a little bit.

00:36:35.900 --> 00:36:36.800
And then I died.

00:36:36.940 --> 00:36:39.580
And then I'm like, oh, I guess that was not supposed to happen.

00:36:39.880 --> 00:36:44.540
Actually, I knew going there that like, oh, I'm probably just way out of my element right now.

00:36:45.180 --> 00:36:53.420
So then I went back and I proceeded to find the first two dungeons and those were relatively easy.

00:36:53.700 --> 00:36:56.260
