00:36:58.980 --> 00:37:03.100
And then I get to the third one and that's a little bit tougher, but I get through that one.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:11.300
And now I'm lost because I didn't even know that there were items hidden in the other dungeons.

00:37:11.300 --> 00:37:14.640
So you hadn't gotten the boomerang or the arrow?

00:37:14.940 --> 00:37:18.360
OK, so I got a boomerang because I think it was just dropped by an enemy.

00:37:18.540 --> 00:37:22.120
Yeah, you have to clear out a whole room and the boomerang will just show up.

00:37:22.220 --> 00:37:25.840
Yeah, but the other ones were like, I didn't even see a screen like that.

00:37:25.940 --> 00:37:30.580
Like that screen where you go down the ladder and then pick up the item and then go back up the ladder.

00:37:30.720 --> 00:37:32.380
Like I never saw that.

00:37:32.440 --> 00:37:36.480
OK, so I that's as much as I played.

00:37:36.920 --> 00:37:40.520
Wow. OK, I mean, I knew that I was missing something.

00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:43.820
But at this point, I didn't have enough time to keep going.

00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:47.220
Right, right, right. And I and I didn't want to look up a walkthrough.

00:37:47.500 --> 00:37:50.660
And I knew that like there was more that I could have done to do this.

00:37:50.780 --> 00:37:56.580
But yeah, I think this is I think this is a counterpoint to I'm not saying that it should be dumbed down.

00:37:56.580 --> 00:38:10.120
But I think it makes more sense design wise to put a barrier in your dungeon that you have to get the item to cross.

00:38:10.320 --> 00:38:13.520
And you'll see them do that in every Zelda game.

00:38:13.520 --> 00:38:20.220
Yeah, it was actually something that felt like it stands out to you almost that like you get an item in the dungeon and need it in another dungeon.

00:38:20.400 --> 00:38:23.460
Like it's like it feels like most games do it the other way.

00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:27.780
It's like weird that you get this raft and like, yes, like I said, it helps you with the very next dungeon.

00:38:27.780 --> 00:38:31.840
But it's like it's weird that it doesn't have any application within the same dungeon.

00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:33.020
And I think that will.

00:38:33.420 --> 00:38:41.800
And yeah, I think that there are positives for having it be like it's not needed and you have to find it in order to progress later.

00:38:41.800 --> 00:38:52.460
But I think if you could if you could like just make sure it'll eliminate it'll eliminate frustration to the people that got into my position.

00:38:53.480 --> 00:39:00.440
