00:40:11.240 --> 00:40:15.100
But my rose colored glasses were telling me, like, I got to go on like a little side quest.

00:40:15.220 --> 00:40:23.220
Like, this will be fun. So I had to go on like another adventure, like, just to figure out, like, back into the dungeon that I already been into and like figure out what did I miss?

00:40:23.280 --> 00:40:24.120
Like, what else was here?

00:40:24.760 --> 00:40:32.240
And something about the fact that, like, I knew, like, I would come in today and talk to you guys and you guys wouldn't have had that same experience I had.

00:40:32.280 --> 00:40:33.200
It was kind of cool to me.

00:40:33.240 --> 00:40:36.160
I was like, you know, we all will have had different adventures.

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:43.860
Yeah. And it's like, I can't think of another example where so far we're like, it's really been the case where it's like we have very different.

00:40:43.960 --> 00:40:45.700
I mean, you know, maybe like branching paths.

00:40:45.880 --> 00:40:50.280
We've been playing very, very limited scope games up until like.

00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:54.920
Right. And this feels like it's just like not just like, oh, I went on a different path or like it was a whole different experience.

00:40:54.920 --> 00:40:56.240
Like I had like a different mission.

00:40:56.480 --> 00:40:57.920
And yeah, I'm talking it up a little bit.

00:40:58.020 --> 00:41:00.420
But I thought that was I thought that was kind of cool.

00:41:00.620 --> 00:41:03.600
Yeah. I kind of have a stray thought just about dungeons in general.

00:41:03.820 --> 00:41:12.680
And that's that I think that I was so appreciative that when I died in a dungeon, they brought me back to the start of the dungeon and not to the start of the overworld.

00:41:12.780 --> 00:41:15.340
Oh, yeah. Because it just kind of I don't know.

00:41:15.340 --> 00:41:25.340
It was it was one of the things that this is the first one of the first games, I think, that I've played where when I die, I don't feel like this is like too hard.

00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:29.660
OK. I feel like it's like it's hard, but it's fair hard.

00:41:29.940 --> 00:41:34.720
You know, like you felt like you shouldn't have been there when you died or you just felt like I earned that death.

00:41:35.540 --> 00:41:37.240
Just like I like I earned it.

00:41:37.380 --> 00:41:42.960
You know, it felt like if like the punishment and rewards of this felt very modern to me.

00:41:43.100 --> 00:41:44.880
It didn't feel like arcade esque.

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:45.780
It is more.

00:41:45.860 --> 00:41:52.700
I mean, I think that we have we've touched upon like having the difficulty feel earned and how like, oh, that death was my fault.

00:41:52.820 --> 00:41:53.660
We've touched upon that.

00:41:53.780 --> 00:41:58.920
Yeah. But in terms of the difficulty of this game where you don't really lose anything when you die.

00:41:59.060 --> 00:41:59.860
Yeah. And that's great.

00:42:00.300 --> 00:42:01.480
And that is very modern.

00:42:01.540 --> 00:42:03.760
I'm not saying it's good or bad, but it is very modern.

00:42:03.760 --> 00:42:14.980
Yeah. And one thing that's very smart with this game that Sam brought up is that it takes you back to the startup screen, you know, like the the place where you found the sword, you know.

00:42:15.280 --> 00:42:24.160
And I think what's smart about that is that if you died in the overworld, that kind of nudges you to say like, oh, maybe I should try a different direction.

00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:26.500
You know, like I was really overwhelmed.

00:42:26.600 --> 00:42:29.820
And you'll know when you're really overwhelmed when you didn't just die because you were being careless.

00:42:29.820 --> 00:42:33.380
Like I was really overwhelmed, like you were saying with the Lynels, you know, like I was being.

00:42:34.320 --> 00:42:35.300
Like rampaged on.

00:42:35.480 --> 00:42:38.460
I need to find a better way to go about this path.

00:42:38.480 --> 00:42:39.880
I'm going to try this way this time.

00:42:39.980 --> 00:42:47.440
You know, it's like that's something neat, because if they would have just loaded you back into like the screen before it, you'd be encouraged to just keep charging back in until it works.

00:42:47.780 --> 00:42:53.660
Yeah. And you it does give you three hearts to start with again when you die, which I think is cool because it's like a little bit of a punishment.

00:42:53.700 --> 00:42:57.100
But it's not like you're as strong as you possibly could be.

00:42:57.280 --> 00:42:59.980
Right. And I like that they respawn all the enemies, too.

00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:01.500
So you have to redo it.

00:43:01.600 --> 00:43:03.360
And it's not like they it's watered down.

00:43:03.360 --> 00:43:08.260
I don't know. I was just really impressed with the with just the feeling it gave me.

00:43:08.460 --> 00:43:17.180
Totally. You know, I think as far as difficulty like on the NES goes, I think this is maybe still more difficult than a lot of games now.

00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:21.160
But I think it like kind of nails that like that perfect medium where it's like not.

00:43:21.340 --> 00:43:25.020
Yeah. It feels difficult, but doable.

00:43:25.820 --> 00:43:28.640
And I like that. I think this for me, this is like the template.

00:43:28.720 --> 00:43:31.000
Like this is what I want other NES games to be like.

00:43:31.320 --> 00:43:41.920
Difficulty wise. And I think one thing to get back to, Joe, since since we're talking about the difficulty and how like things aren't necessarily spelled out for you and everybody has different paths is that that was completely Miyamoto's intention.

